# existed and that this gate could not see. They were TRIAGED, not blanket-
# baselined; the triage rule is stated once here and every row below obeys it.
#
# THE RULE. The SCOPE of a row must equal the SCOPE of the reason justifying it.
#   * A reason that is structural for a whole file (Go excludes *_test.go from
#     every production build) earns a file+class row.
#   * A reason that is about one literal (this string is a vendor API id, not a
#     machine binding) earns a row pinned to that literal.
#   * Anything that is neither is DEBT: a BASELINE row with an AUDIT.md id.
# CLASS is never widened to `*` in this section, so a NEW finding of a DIFFERENT
# class in an already-covered file still fails the gate.
#
# WHAT IS JUSTIFIED, and on what evidence:
#   (A) *_test.go — `go build` excludes these files from every production
#       binary, so no literal in them can configure a deployment. Measured
#       2026-09-01: 28 of the 30 test files carrying findings drive
#       httptest.NewServer; the other two use a deliberately unreachable port
#       (127.0.0.1:1) or assert a constructor default, and their single live
#       path is capability-guarded and t.Skip()s. Making these values
#       environment-derived would delete the assertion.
#   (B) FallbackModels / SupportedModels entries — the last-resort list used
#       ONLY when the live ModelsEndpoint discovery call fails. Measured
#       2026-09-01: all 107 non-test MODEL list elements sit inside
#       `FallbackModels: []string{` (106) or `SupportedModels: []string{` (1);
#       not one is a default selection. This is precisely the shape the gate
#       own isfallback heuristic exempts - the heuristic is single-line and
#       cannot see the field name three lines above the literal. The detector
#       was deliberately NOT widened to compensate: widening a detector to
#       reach rc=0 is the failure mode this section exists to avoid.
#   (C) zen.go exported model-id constants - a named catalog with deprecation
#       notes, for callers to pass in. The only default, DefaultZenModel, is a
#       symbol reference and never fires.
#   (D) pattern false positives on the token `codestral`: a provider id, a Go
#       variable name codestralResp, an i18n message key, an English
#       description string. None is a model id.
#
# WHAT IS DEBT: F23-F28 in docs/environment-adaptability/AUDIT.md. Each is a
# real defect. NONE of them can be fixed from this repository - they live in
# other repositories and 11.4.29 forbids editing a tree this repository does not
